# Build context for backend/Dockerfile (ticket E0-02).
#
# Deny everything, then name what the build needs. The other way round — listing
# what to exclude — fails open: a file added later is in the context until
# someone remembers to exclude it, and `.env` is the file that matters most. It
# is gitignored, so it exists on every developer's machine and in CI, and a
# `COPY . .` would put a real credential into an image layer. Starting from `*`
# makes that impossible rather than unlikely.

*

!pyproject.toml
!README.md
!requirements.txt
!requirements-dev.txt
!backend

# Re-included above with the directory; none of it belongs in an image.
backend/**/__pycache__
backend/**/*.py[cod]
backend/*.egg-info
